# ACT Configuration for local GitHub Actions testing
# https://github.com/nektos/act

# The image act runs ubuntu-latest jobs in: Node 24 (package.json engines)
# with jq, gh and docker, as GitHub's runners have them. Build it first:
#   docker build --platform linux/amd64 -t claret-act:24 .github/act
--platform ubuntu-latest=claret-act:24

# A local image, which no registry has: act pulls images by default.
--pull=false

# Container architecture for Apple Silicon compatibility
--container-architecture linux/amd64

# Enable verbose output for debugging
# --verbose

# No host Docker socket in the job containers: act binds it by default,
# and code in a job could then mount any folder Docker Desktop shares, the
# home directory included. The one job step that needs Docker, actionlint,
# runs on the host under act (npm run lint:workflows).
--container-daemon-socket -

# An empty GITHUB_TOKEN: without the key, act fills it from `gh auth token`,
# your repo-scoped login, and hands it to every job. A run that needs a token
# passes -s GITHUB_TOKEN=... itself.
--secret GITHUB_TOKEN=

# No secret file by default: .env.act.local holds real tokens, and no
# rehearsal needs them. A run that does passes --secret-file .env.act.local.

# Custom event file location (optional)
# --eventpath .github/workflows/events/